readme = "# A shared digital site plan\n\nThe idea is to let channel, regional image information and drilling track share precise image, axis and dimensions. The code searches length/diameter and shows which queries can actually be determined. All data is local and the parent operators are called unchanged.\n\n```bash\n./run_all.sh\n```\n\nRequires existing neighbor packages and their hashbound small raw files on the data disk, Python3 with NumPy / SciPy, as well as system-Python with Matplotlib. Execution uses a wire, no GPU or network access; no ZIP is unpacked. Executable benchmark, not standalone public product.\n\n| Results | Outcome | Resolution |\n|---|---:|---|\n| Samlade platsrapporter |2581,433 fall|PER_TOOTH|\n| Close channel versions + bone at exactly the same pose |22 sites , 4 case|PER_POINT→PER_TOOTH|\n| Tested Dimensions |330|PER_TOOTH|\n| Fully guided 95% scenario with digital selection |18/22|POPULATION, conditional on the model|\n| Originally passed digital 2 mm margin lost at 1,5 mm extra drill depth |15/21|POPULATION, prescribed scenario|\n| Physically calibrated Comprehensive Plans |0/2581|POPULATION|\n\n![Result and Drill Line](figures/site_plan.png)\n\n[SITE_PLANS .jsonl](SITE_PLANS .jsonl) is the overall delivery. [POPULATION_TABLE.csv ](POPULATION_TABLE.csv) has guides × segments × goal with image bootstrap-KI . [Research commands](raw/RESEARCH_CHOICES_R2.json) retains Pareto-candidates and margins. [Borr limits](raw/DRILL_LIMITS_R3.json) indicates numeric search intervals, and [exports](export/GEOMETRY.json) binds STL /channel points to the original frame. [RESULTS.md ](RESULTS.md) contains exactly reference and limitations.\n\n**What is not holds :** bone profiles are uncalibrated gray values, regional housing samples include teeth, poses are virtual dentata test sites, channel versions are not independent anatomical annotations and guide distributions tails are not validated. No nerve injury risk , safe patient dimension, under-drilling, thermal dose, fatigue survival or Ti/Zr recommendation can be derived. A failed conservative margin condition is not a measured injury. Numerical examinations on 0,01 mm do not imply anatomical accuracy on 0,01 mm.\n\nExternally digital reference : the original masks preserved local voxlar in X73 , original CBCT profiles in X75 , guide observations via X87 . Clinical counter-test: [Bartling1999 ](https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/10596660/) 8/94 early sensory changes (primary, not table calibration), [Jamil2020 Tables1/2/4 ](https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC7137271/#Tab4) 9/80 positions below the intended 2 mm margin and five symptom cases in separate text. These groups are not our CBCT patients and their frequencies must not be mixed with our digital decisions.\n\nBefore future manufacturing/measurement there is [FROZEN_PREDICTIONS.json ](FROZEN_PREDICTIONS.json) with hash and time stamp. It is goal for a geometric laboratory specimen , not completed physical validation. The next crucial measurement is planned/achieved pose and independent canal wall in the same frame; then co-located bore/moment/temperature measurement .\n\nDataset licenses: ToothFairy2 CC BY-SA4.0 according to local dataset.json ; ToothFairy CC BY - SA according to [dataset owner](https://toothfairy.grand-challenge.org/dataset/), exact version not verified here. Maxillo's separate license is  UNKNOWN ; derivation is maintained  local  and are not distributed. Publications retain the respective license/copyright. No Teeth3DS, Bits2Bites, mandible defect or MMDental data are used; no records or personal data are processed. Image-ID is published anonymized dataset-ID .\n\nStatus: PENDING_INDEPENDENT_REVIEW. All old failures, source hashs, costs and the next measurement are in results.json/HANDOFF.md.\n"
(P / 'README_DEMO.md').write_text(readme)
